      "snippet": "After a long period of comparative neglect, in the last few decades growing numbers of philosophers have been paying attention to the startling contrast presented between Kant\u2019s universal moral theory, with its inspiring enlightenment ideas of human autonomy, equality and dignity and Kant\u2019s racism. Against Charles Mills, who argues that the way to make Kant consistent is by attributing to him a threshold notion of moral personhood, according to which some races do not qualify for consideration under the categorical imperative, I argue that Kant cannot be made consistent on race, and that rather than trying to make him so, we should use the example of Kant\u2019s racism to tell us something about the nature of racism.",
